  "body": "**Blocked by:** #137, #84\n\n## Context\n\nThe core schema contains foreign keys to `users`, but the existing user row is only a placeholder. This issue establishes the persistent authentication model used by every later slice in this batch.\n\n## Task\n\nCreate migrations for `users(id,email,password_hash,locale,created_at)`, `sessions(id,user_id,token_hash,platform,created_at,last_seen_at,expires_at,user_agent,revoked_at)`, and `login_attempts(id,email,ip,succeeded,attempted_at)` with the constraints and indexes needed for unique email, unique token hash, expiry/revocation lookup, and recent email-plus-IP failures. Preserve multiple sessions per user. Add shared primitives that hash passwords with Argon2id, generate cryptographically random opaque tokens, store only token hashes, and compare secrets without timing-sensitive string equality. Do not introduce JWTs.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Schema, migrations, TypeScript types, repositories, Argon2id and opaque-token primitives.\n- `users.locale` defaulting to `cs`; platforms restricted to `web`, `ios`, or `macos`.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- HTTP login and session middleware, delivered by #140.\n- Reset and setup flows.\n- Multi-user authorization and `resource_grants` behavior.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A migration from the current placeholder user schema preserves existing referenced user IDs and produces the complete schema.\n- Two sessions can reference one user; duplicate email and duplicate token hash are rejected.\n- Tests demonstrate Argon2id verification and that neither raw passwords nor raw session tokens are persisted.\n",
